    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0052" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/25878: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-21T15:00:00-04:00">November 21,
                            1942—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2027. The Foreign Office repeating its pledges that Chile will break relations
                    gently requests, as had General Escudero and Morales,<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d49-f1"/> that as much as possible of the armament our Under
                    Secretary indicated to Ambassador Michels could be given to Chile (Department’s
                    1380, November 14, 11 p.m.) be sent with the least possible delay and not be
                    withheld until rupture actually takes place, arguing that it would relieve
                    military fears, enhance good feeling in the army, and be accepted as a
                    gratifying expression of confidence in Chile’s pledge to break with the Axis. I
                    urgently support this request.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d49-f1" n="54" xml:id="d49-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably Raúl Morales Beltrami, Chilean Minister of the Interior.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
